.TH MOUSE_DOWN 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
mouse_down \- True while the mouse button is held
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqinput.h\(dq
.BI "bool mouse_down(const Input *in, MouseButton b);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
True while the mouse button is held. Position is in\->mouse_x / in\->mouse_y in logical pixels, so comparing it against a Rect you drew is exact regardless of window size; use rect_contains() for the test. For a world\-space position under a camera, convert with camera_to_world().
.PP
This is a static inline function; it is defined in the header.
.SH RETURN VALUE
true if button b is held this frame.
.SH MODULE
input (src/engine/input/input.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mouse_pressed (3),
.BR mouse_released (3),
.BR rect_contains (3),
.BR camera_to_world (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
